[center][size=6][b][color=#f5c542]Cyrillic Fonts[/color][/b][/size]
[size=3][i]The game's own fonts — now with Cyrillic. Russian and Ukrainian finally look like the rest of the game.[/i][/size]

[size=2]Version 1.0.0 · The Spell Brigade 1.2 · MelonLoader 0.7[/size][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#f5c542]The problem[/color][/b][/size]

The game's fonts — [b]Irish Grover[/b] for headings and buttons, [b]Titillium Web[/b] for everything else — have no Cyrillic letters. So in Russian and Ukrainian every text falls back to a plain default font: "OPTIONS" becomes a thin "НАСТРОЙКИ", "READY" turns into an ordinary "ГОТОВ", and the menus lose their character.

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#f5c542]What the mod does[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Headings and buttons in Irish Grover[/b] — Cyrillic letters built from the font's own glyphs: shared shapes are reused as-is (А, В, Е, К, М, Н, О, Р, С, Т, Х), the rest are mirrored, flipped and assembled from its own strokes and serifs (И, Я, Г, П, Ж, Ш, Д…).
[*][b]All other text in Titillium Web[/b] — the very same font the game uses, with Cyrillic added (Titillium Web [RUS by Daymarius]). Every weight is matched: ExtraLight, Light, Regular, SemiBold, Bold.
[*][b]Latin stays original[/b] — the mod only fills in letters the game's fonts are missing, so English and other Latin-script languages don't change at all.
[*][b]Russian and Ukrainian[/b] — all letters including Ё, Ґ, Є, І, Ї.
[*][b]Same size and outline[/b] — Cyrillic is scaled to the height of the original capitals and uses the game's own text shader, so outlines and shadows look the same.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#f5c542]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://github.com/LavaGang/MelonLoader/releases]MelonLoader[/url] (0.7.x) for The Spell Brigade and launch the game once.
[*]Put [b]CyrillicFonts.dll[/b] into [font=Courier New]<Game folder>\Mods\[/font] (the fonts are inside the dll).
[*]Launch the game with the Russian or Ukrainian language.
[/list]

[b]Settings[/b] are in [font=Courier New]UserData\MelonPreferences.cfg[/font], section [font=Courier New][CyrillicFonts][/font]: [b]Enabled[/b], and [b]HeadingScale[/b] / [b]TextScale[/b] to make Cyrillic a bit bigger or smaller if you prefer.

[line]

[size=5][b][color=#f5c542]FAQ[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Does it change anything in English?[/b]
No. The added letters are only used where the game's fonts have none.

[b]Does it work in co-op?[/b]
Yes. It's purely visual and local; other players don't need it.

[b]How do I uninstall?[/b]
Delete [b]CyrillicFonts.dll[/b] from the Mods folder (and, if you like, the [font=Courier New]UserData\CyrillicFonts[/font] folder).

[line]

